The current failing code (from the spec read at ledger 206):
```typescript
const productArticles = page.locator("mat-grid-tile mat-card");
await expect(productArticles.first()).toBeVisible();
const count = await productArticles.count();
expect(count).toBeGreaterThan(0);
for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {
  const nameButton = productArticles.nth(i).locator("button").first();
  await expect(nameButton).toContainText(/apple/i);
}
```

From the page snapshot, articles contain `button "Click for more information about the product"` with text like "Apple Juice (1000ml)". The correct approach: use `page.locator("article")` and check the button text inside each.

Also, AC-2 needs to assert both the transition and the term shown. The current AC-2 only asserts `getByText("apple")` is visible. I need to also assert the heading "Search Results - apple" to prove transition.

